<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Bernburg</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Bernburg is a town on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saale">Saale</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saxony-anhalt">Saxony-Anhalt</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a>. Its <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/renaissance">Renaissance</a> castle on a rock above the river was the residence of the princes, later dukes, of Anhalt-Bernburg from 1603 until the line died out in 1863. The town then became part of the united Duchy of Anhalt and later grew as a centre of salt and chemical industry.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/bernburg.jpg" alt="Bernburg" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: FrankBothe · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Herbststimmung_in_Bernburg.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
